      "sequenced_unit_plan": "Sequenced unit plan",
      "set_0_05_very_tight_inheritance_and_ru": "Set σ = 0.05 (very tight inheritance) and run 5 drought years. Compare with σ = 0.40 (loose inheritance). Lower mutation = slower response to selection because there's less variation to work with.",
      "set_a_population_size_then_run_5_paral": "Set a population size, then run 5 parallel lineages. They all start at p = 0.5 (50/50 allele frequencies) and evolve only by chance — no selection, no mutation. Smaller populations drift much harder.",
      "set_mutation_size_to_0_12_high_the_dyn": "Set Mutation Size to 0.12 (high). The dynamics get noisier but the arms race speeds up. Real mutation rates are lower; here exaggerated to be visible on the timescale of a classroom session.",
